## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- a10 and a21, and the «بیشترین» half of a14, treat the R3 advertising hedges as mistranslations and ask to put the concrete sentence or the high result back. Those hedges are the standing rule. The 3/4/6-month distinction and the “not guaranteed” sentence were already present; B’s anecdote already stops at statutory entitlement.
- a24 and b18 treat the zero-width spacers, the empty bold lines, and Q16–Q20 as body lines as a Persian layout defect. They are copied from the Korean source and the checker counts them. Removing them, or promoting Q16–Q20 to headings, fails checkBlocks / checkHeadings.
- b23 asks to close a heading-number gap the English source also has. Renumbering would diverge from that source and would change a number.
